{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261027T223059Z-ae6cb24e", "ts": "2026-10-27T22:33:07Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.0-dev.2", "branch": "fix/briefing-banner"}, "body": {"base_commit": "eb4de60ea330e0d9cfc8e1a40665936e76b2d2ad", "base_tree": "d28058350bc526e7fcfae56e34065884436ebebd", "head_tree": "aeafb65ad8fb0adc8272c7bdeab56eabcfe2ae1a", "head_commit": "2064bba0ef171b785b4aed667d7e9d390a767ab8", "dispatch_commit": "2064bba0ef171b785b4aed667d7e9d390a767ab8", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/hooks/banner.py", "plugin/lib/briefing.py", "plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py", "plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md", "tests/test_briefing_functions.py", "tests/test_plan_lifecycle.py", "tests/test_plugin_version_banner.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/changes/briefing-banner.md", "plugin/hooks/banner.py", "plugin/lib/briefing.py", "plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py", "plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md", "tests/test_briefing_functions.py", "tests/test_plan_lifecycle.py", "tests/test_plugin_version_banner.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/changes/briefing-banner.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "The downgrade banner reads the rolled-back range from the older plugin's own CHANGELOG and gates.json, which do not contain it, so it lists nothing and then relays 'what was rolled back above'", "recommendation": "render_delta gets `root = plugin_root()`, which is the plugin now running. After a downgrade that is the OLDER tree. Its CHANGELOG.md has no section for any version above its own, and its hooks/gates.json has no gate whose `since` is above its own version. So `highlights_in_range(parse_changelog(root), current, last)` and `new_gates_in_range(parse_gates(root), current, last)` are empty in practice. The banner prints only the `\u2193` line, followed by '\u21d2 Tell the user what was rolled back above', with nothing above it. The fragment's claim that the banner 'lists the rolled-back range's changelog highlights \u2026 and its gates as no longer enforced' does not hold outside the test. `_rollback_root` builds a single fixture tree that contains the newer v2.1.0 entry and the later-gate, a tree no real downgrade has, so the test passes. Fix: when the downgrade lists nothing, use a relay line that refers to nothing above it, e.g. 'Tell the user the plugin was rolled back from vA to vB'. Either drop the range listing, or source it from somewhere that actually holds the newer versions. Replace the fixture with a tree whose CHANGELOG and gates stop at the older version, and pin that output.", "files": ["plugin/hooks/banner.py", "tests/test_plugin_version_banner.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "note", "title": "The off-base test withdraws a true merge that was made locally and not yet pushed, when the plan declares no `base:`", "recommendation": "With no declared base, `base_refs` holds only the one ref `coverage.repo_base_branch` resolves, which is `origin/<b>` by preference (#311). Take a plan merged into local `develop`, not pushed, with its branch deleted. It is committed at HEAD and absent from `origin/develop`'s tree, so `_committed_off_base` returns True. The pending-fragment inference that answered merged-unreleased before this change now gives `unknown`. For that window the briefing says 'Fix the frontmatter' and check-claims reports it missing. The module docstring treats 'a merge made locally is on `<base>` before it is pushed' as a merge. Consider also checking the bare local `<b>` in `_committed_off_base`, or accept the window on the record.", "files": ["plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "plan_lifecycle's 'Cost (NF1)' accounting does not count the new cat-file probes", "recommendation": "The module docstring lists step 5's git calls precisely: one `--contains` per anchor. The new `_committed_off_base` adds up to 1 + len(base_refs) `git cat-file -e` calls whenever a pending record would otherwise answer. Add them to the Cost paragraph. The spy tests pin call lists only for other paths, so nothing would flag the drift.", "files": ["plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "_committed_off_base treats an untracked plan as no evidence, so the briefing now goes silent on a fresh, uncommitted plan with a mistyped branch", "recommendation": "The pending-record inference is withdrawn only when the plan is committed at HEAD and missing from every base tree. An untracked plan returns False, and the docstring calls that 'withdrawing it on no evidence'. But an untracked plan file is evidence: a merge brings committed files, so a plan that is on disk and in no commit cannot have merged. Before this change that polarity only affected `plan status`. Now staleness_scan asks the lifecycle (_past_its_merge), so it has a user-visible effect: right after `plan new` writes the plan and its fragment, a session start or /clear before the first commit reads a mistyped `branch:` as merged-unreleased. The briefing drops the 'not a branch in this repo' line, and doctor's check-claims prints 'archive at the release'. That is the case #1106's control test exists for, one step earlier in time. The existing TestBranchGone test for a pending fragment inferring merged-unreleased builds its 'merged' plan as an untracked file, which no real merge produces. The False-on-untracked default seems to keep that fixture green rather than describe reality. Fix (instance): when the plan path is inside the repo and missing from HEAD and from every base tree, withdraw the inference. Keep False only for a path outside the repo or when git cannot answer. Then commit the plan in the merged-case fixture so it matches a real merge.", "files": ["plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py", "plugin/lib/briefing.py", "tests/test_plan_lifecycle.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "The banner's glyph inventory and render_delta's docstring still describe an upgrade-only delta", "recommendation": "The RELAY_MARKER comment lists the banner's line glyphs as `\u2191`/`\u2022`/`\u2295`. render_delta now also emits `\u2193`, `\u2212` and `\u2296`, and its docstring talks only about announcing an upgrade. highlights_in_range's 'Empty on a downgrade' is still literally true, but render_delta now calls it with the bounds swapped on purpose. Nothing reads this prose. Make the glyph sentence relational ('the delta block's own line glyphs') rather than an enumeration, or leave it as is. Scope: instance.", "files": ["plugin/hooks/banner.py"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Doctor check 24's new 'when' clause attaches ambiguously", "recommendation": "Framework Check 8 (Instruction Clarity). '...or a pending fragment (or, on a single-file log, an untagged entry) when the plan is not committed only on an unmerged branch' can be read as qualifying the whole list of release-pending evidence. In the code, the off-base guard applies only to the pending-record inference, though to both kinds of record. The relay instructions are unaffected, so this is a NOTE. If it is edited, attach the condition directly to 'a pending change record'. Scope: instance.", "files": ["plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner (no plan governs this branch)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. No live plan claims fix/briefing-banner, so the record of these decisions is the fragment and the code comments. (1) When either version fails to parse, or the two sort equal, the banner says 'Prawduct changed' instead of guessing a direction. (2) A downgrade still relays, and it lists the range being left as removed (highlights_in_range/new_gates_in_range called with current, last). (3) The briefing goes quiet only when the lifecycle says merged-unreleased, released or superseded. unknown and in-progress keep the nag. (4) The pending-record inference in plan_lifecycle.observe is narrowed: it is withdrawn when the plan is committed at HEAD and appears in no base tree. This changes what plan status, plan check-claims and doctor report as well as the briefing. The fragment's consumer note records it, and the merged-and-deleted case, the mistyped-branch case and the untracked-plan case are all pinned. Each decision traces to #1104 or #1106 and is reachable from its caller. Owner: veto any of these at merge if you disagree.", "files": ["plugin/hooks/banner.py", "plugin/lib/briefing.py", "plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "prawduct-hook's check-claims docstring still lists 'a pending change record for the scope' as unconditional merge evidence", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The cause is that the narrowed inference in plan_lifecycle.observe was carried into doctor SKILL.md step 24 and the module docstring, but not into _cmd_plan_check_claims's docstring in plugin/bin/prawduct-hook (the release-pending bullet, around line 8651). Core rule 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees' applies. Nothing reads this docstring to make a decision. A maintainer reading it would expect a pending fragment to always mean release-pending, which is wrong for a plan committed only on an unmerged branch. Either add the same qualifier SKILL.md now carries, or make the bullet relational ('the lifecycle plan status prints') and drop the enumeration.", "files": ["plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "RELAY_MARKER's comment lists the banner's line glyphs as \u2191/\u2022/\u2295, but the downgrade path adds \u2193/\u2212/\u2296", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. This is inert prose, and no edit is wanted unless the line is touched anyway. The comment above RELAY_MARKER in banner.py enumerates the glyphs, and the new downgrade branch adds three that the comment does not name. If it is touched, make it relational ('alongside the banner's own line glyphs') rather than extending the list.", "files": ["plugin/hooks/banner.py"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: no regression of a loaded rule found", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Read list from learnings-files --for-diff: core, authoring, gates, hook-surface, release, tests. Checked against tests.md 'When a fix NARROWS a detector, the verification set must include the TRUE POSITIVES'. Both narrowings pin a true positive: test_a_mistyped_branch_on_unmerged_work_still_nags for the briefing, and the untracked-plan sibling that still infers for the lifecycle. Checked against 'A comment that NAMES a new failure mode owes a test'. The untracked case in _committed_off_base's docstring is pinned; the path-outside-repo and HEAD-unreadable branches are fail-soft returns of False and are not separately pinned. The only rule-bearing finding is the docstring NOTE above, under core's 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees'. No rules were added or changed this cycle.", "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: #1104 banner: update banner calls a version downgrade an upgrade", "recommendation": "Scope: none. render_delta now distinguishes upgrade, downgrade and an unorderable move, and the fragment's closes: names #1104. Verify it, then call /prawduct:backlog update 1104 status=shipped closed-by=scope:briefing-banner when the backlog skill's 'When to mark shipped' rule says.", "files": ["plugin/hooks/banner.py"], "fid": "R-11"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: #1106 governance: stale-plan briefing nags merged-unreleased plans", "recommendation": "Scope: none. staleness_scan now asks plan_lifecycle.observe and stays silent for a plan past its merge. The fragment's closes: names #1106. Verify it, then call /prawduct:backlog update 1106 status=shipped closed-by=scope:briefing-banner when the backlog skill's 'When to mark shipped' rule says.", "files": ["plugin/lib/briefing.py"], "fid": "R-12"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "C-B3: open #1079 (dirty-tree chunk review reads open after its plan merges) is masked on the briefing surface, not resolved", "recommendation": "Scope: none. backlog cache-query affecting returns #1079, #755 and #928 for the changed files. This change stops #1079's chunk-state defect from reaching the stale-plan message, but chunk_states still reads such a chunk as open, so the item stays open. Assess whether its text should now name the remaining surfaces. #755 and #928 are untouched by this diff.", "files": ["plugin/lib/briefing.py"], "fid": "R-13"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Records Pass: .prawduct/changes/briefing-banner.md clears no bar", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The set covered is files_oracle = [.prawduct/changes/briefing-banner.md]. Each claim was checked against the code. Downgrade rendering, the 'Prawduct changed' branch, relay, the lifecycle states that silence the briefing, the 'committed at HEAD and absent from every base tree' condition, and 'unknown' for the mistyped-branch plan all match banner.py, briefing.py, plan_lifecycle.py and their tests. Nothing in it ships false, misleads into action or should stop the merge. record_lint reported zero findings.", "files": [".prawduct/changes